          "matched_text": "set aside",
          "start": 44,
          "end": 53
        }
      ],
      "text_preview": "This Court by the judgment dated 09.09.2015 set aside the judgment under challenge and remanded the matter to the Tribunal with direction to implead respondent Nos.4 to 6 in the case and for reconsideration of the matter thereafter."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "62e9d6015a51445d8b68e7f8abd2293e_52",
      "summary_section": "facts",
      "labels": [
        "RLC"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_labels:RLC"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "7. The Tribunal on hearing the parties by the impugned award held that both driver of the lorry and Tempo Traveller contributed 50% each in occurrence of accident."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "33f60591965d49759b9a54209841a4d0_53",
      "summary_section": "facts",
      "labels": [
        "RLC"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_labels:RLC"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The Tribunal considered permanent physical disability of the claimant at 25%, assessed his income at Rs.2,80,000/- per annum, applied 13 multiplier and assessed his future income at Rs.9,10,000/-."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "a817535355574950b7071458dc5e1068_54",
      "summary_section": "facts",
      "labels": [
        "RLC"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_labels:RLC"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The Tribunal in all awarded compensation of Rs.21,00,000/- on different heads as below:\nSri Kumar B C vs Sri Manjunatha on 27 November, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/54344009/\n5"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "852b67c60e4d45d9b7391138cd8f8bfa_66",
      "summary_section": "facts",
      "labels": [
        "FAC"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "explicit_leakage_phrase"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [
        {
          "pattern": "\\bset\\s+aside\\b",
          "matched_text": "set aside",
          "start": 129,
          "end": 138
        }
      ],
      "text_preview": "Therefore, finding of the Tribunal on the point of negligence is contrary to the evidence on record and the same is liable to be set aside."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "000bb6e1bfe7463c98ac1f7a67c6c10b_74",
      "summary_section": "facts",
      "labels": [
        "RLC"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_labels:RLC"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Therefore, the Tribunal was justified in fixing 50% liability to the insurer of Tempo Traveller vehicle."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "05dcebacbb114e53a11515801752b6fa_77",
      "summary_section": "issue",
      "labels": [
        "ISSUE"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:issue"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "On considering the submissions of both side and on examining the materials on record, the questions that arise for determination of this Court are:\n\"i. Whether the finding of the Tribunal that drivers of Tempo Traveller bearing registration"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "d728ee5710df4544b5bbb1bdfc1dbad5_78",
      "summary_section": "issue",
      "labels": [
        "ISSUE"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:issue"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Whether compensation awarded under the impugned award is just one?\""
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "cadf836d465247c2bbf6ce8b2e1c4927_79",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "\nAnalysis Reg. Negligence:\n11. Parties have not disputed that on 07.08.2012 at 12:45 a.m., when claimant was traveling in Tempo Traveller bearing registration No.K.A-01-AB-2638, an accident took place involving the said Tempo Traveller and "
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "ee3662f076ea4fb5822c4b336b14ae8f_80",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "It is also not disputed that regarding the accident, Ms.Shilpa-family member of the claimant, filed complaint as per Ex.P1 against the driver of the lorry."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "7c426782403c490fa2a9e3c1e31f9313_84",
      "summary_section": "facts",
      "labels": [
        "RLC"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_labels:RLC"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Learned Magistrate convicted and sentenced him for the offences punishable under Sections, 279,337,338 IPC and 134(a)(b) read with Section 187 MV Act."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "526b21801f07470e8756feb15da106a6_85",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "By such evidence, there was prima-facie proof of occurrence of accident due to actionable negligence on the part of the driver of the lorry."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "71e4a48c79844472b2894ad98ba3f2ce_86",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "It is no doubt true that those documents were not conclusive proof, but they have some presumptive value under Section 114 illustration (e) of Evidence Act."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "e2f455de9bcf4fccb5671c750086ee69_87",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Therefore, it was for respondent Nos.1 and 2 to adduce evidence to rebut the said presumption."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "51368b1014374271a653bbb4bd35f427_88",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Insurer of lorry /respondent No.2 had challenged first award of the Tribunal before this Court in MFA No.5268/2014 C/w MFA No.6048/2014 on the same ground."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "9ac838d72f1c4a389e8f80f23babe56e_89",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "This Court on setting aside the order of Tribunal, remanded the matter for fresh consideration, reserving liberty to the parties to lead evidence."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "02ca7c4fffaf49c19e50213849c41526_90",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Even thereafter respondent Nos.1 and 2 did not avail the said opportunity to lead evidence."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "b292ace2352f45cc9ea57a22e986b8a9_91",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "\n12. Regulation No.8 of the Regulations,1989 state that whenever a driver of the motor vehicle is nearing a road - 12 - NC: 2024:KHC:48704-DB intersection, pedestrian crossing, or road junction, he shall not enter such intersection, junctio"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "6e1ddbfc991d4cb5b59cb8b2cc619374_92",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Regulation No.9 of the Regulations,1989 is to the same effect relating to junction where the traffic is not being regulated."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "6fed7fca52204703aa40eb2bdfc0ca5a_93",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "It says he has to give way to all traffic approaching the intersection on his right hand."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "99c8c66c4238463eacb91b9a61ad72e5_94",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Before this Court it is being contended that the driver of the Tempo Traveller entered the road without taking any due care as required under Regulation Nos.8 and 9 of the Regulations,1989."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "f101bcaf28b746a9a04c12706b7b11bc_95",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The sketch/Ex.P3 shows that lorry has proceeded from its extreme right side to extreme left side."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "060ed70f746b4c0cbaf1664639871911_96",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "When driver of the lorry pleaded guilty, it was for respondent Nos.1 to 3 to enter witness box and claim that driver of Tempo Traveller was negligent."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "e0bfef60ba014b009869a0ac6733ed87_97",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "\nBut they did not defend the case at all, nor respondent Nos.1 and 2 examined respondent No.3/driver of lorry."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "4e08893bfdda4454b3a8da0ecfbf1835_98",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "That amounts to suppression of available material evidence, which leads to drawing of adverse inference against respondent Nos.1 to 3."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "e0c426b91805461cb97d787cfa87e161_99",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The Tribunal without assigning any acceptable reasons has come to the conclusion that the drivers of both vehicles have contributed to the occurrence of accident, which is wholly unsustainable."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "d8170c8253fc4e05a6574593c7b2a703_100",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS",
        "explicit_leakage_phrase"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [
        {
          "pattern": "\\bset\\s+aside\\b",
          "matched_text": "set aside",
          "start": 68,
          "end": 77
        }
      ],
      "text_preview": "Hence, the said finding requires - 13 - NC: 2024:KHC:48704-DB to be set aside and the entire culpable negligence has to be imputed to respondent No.3 and vicariously respondent No.1."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "7d8a7fcdef144ff38cc05f115f0ad333_101",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Reg. Quantum:\nSri Kumar B C vs Sri Manjunatha on 27 November, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/54344009/\n8 13."
    },
    {
